# What NOT to upload to EAS Build.
#
# The 1.0.58 build shipped a 1000 MB archive and spent 5m27s uploading it,
# every time. Almost all of that was local Gradle output: android/app/build is
# 2.3 GB on disk and android/app/.cxx another 336 MB, none of which EAS can
# use - it compiles from scratch in the cloud.
#
# IMPORTANT: when this file exists, EAS uses it INSTEAD OF .gitignore, not in
# addition to it. Anything that needs excluding has to be listed here even if
# .gitignore already covers it. That is why node_modules is repeated below;
# leaving it out would upload 4.7 GB.

# Dependencies - EAS runs its own install
node_modules/

# Android build output and caches
android/build/
android/app/build/
android/app/.cxx/
android/.gradle/
android/.kotlin/
android/local.properties

# iOS build output
ios/build/
ios/Pods/
ios/*.xcworkspace/xcuserdata/
ios/*.xcodeproj/xcuserdata/

# Expo / Metro caches
.expo/
.expo-shared/
web-build/

# Previously built artifacts
*.apk
*.aab
*.hprof

# The Google Play Developer API key. `eas submit` reads it from the LOCAL
# machine, never from the build archive, so uploading it only widens where a
# credential that can publish to the store has been.
play-service-account.json

# Local tooling noise
coverage/
*.log
.DS_Store
.vscode/
.idea/

# NOT excluded on purpose:
#   credentials.json and android/app/*.keystore - the production profile uses
#   credentialsSource: local, and signing must not break to save a few KB.
